@TUTORIAL: Following a Job                      !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  You have submitted a job, MYJOB. Where is it now? Type ST on the
}  command line: the Status panel lists it with all the others you may
}  see. Its QUEUE field tells where it is:
}
{  INPUT      }read in, waiting for an initiator of its class. POS is
}               its place in line, 1 the first; a held job has none.
{  EXECUTION  }running. The row is white.
{  PRINT      }ended; its output waits to be printed, or is held.
}
}  If the list is long, find your job with FIND:
{    F MYJOB    }the row of MYJOB goes to the top.
}  Or show only your jobs: ST MYJOB, or ST MY* for all names that begin
}  with MY (part 6).
}
}  Press Enter to see the Status panel.
}
}
}
}
}
